annota (0.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Screen recording: record a region, a window or the whole screen through
    the ScreenCast portal and PipeWire, with a countdown, a recording
    control (pause, stop, mute microphone and system audio) and the Record
    shortcut (Super+Alt+R preferred) or `annota --record`. Export to MP4
    (H.264 + AAC) or WebM (VP9 + Opus); recordings survive a crash.
  * Window captures contain the whole window at its on-screen size on
    scaled displays (they held only the top-left part at 125 %).
  * The pointer is drawn where it is in delayed region captures and in
    screen captures.
  * Region captures with "Include pointer" draw the pointer where it is at
    confirmation.
  * zip 9.8.1 (security fixes); Rust 1.91 is the minimum toolchain, Debian 13
    is no longer a build platform.
  * New runtime dependencies for recording: gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
    -ugly and -bad.

 -- Thorsten Rosin <thorsten.rosin@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

annota (0.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First release.
  * Capture a region, a window or the whole screen through
    xdg-desktop-portal, with delay, pointer and multi-monitor options and
    global shortcuts (GlobalShortcuts portal, or GNOME custom keybindings).
  * Window stills through the ScreenCast portal's window chooser and
    GStreamer.
  * Editor with arrows, shapes, pen, text, callouts, numbered steps,
    highlighter and redaction; every annotation stays editable, with
    undo/redo, crop, resize, rotate and the editable .annota format.
  * Quick styles, themes and tool presets.
  * Export to PNG, JPG, WebP and PDF, copy to the clipboard and drag out.
  * English and German.

 -- Thorsten Rosin <thorsten.rosin@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100

